        "Figure 1: Fano planes of three octonionic subalgebras in the sedenions."
      ],
      "labels": [
        {
          "text": "Sedenions, Cℓ(8), and three generations of fermions",
          "bbox": [
            83.34,
            52.65,
            292.18,
            65.02
          ],
          "intersectsDrawing": false,
          "fonts": [
            "CMMI10",
            "CMR10",
            "MSBM10",
            "NimbusRomNo9L-Regu",
            "NimbusRomNo9L-ReguItal"
          ],
          "sizes": [
            9.96
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Niels G. Gresnigt",
          "bbox": [
            441.93,
            55.05,
            511.94,
            65.02
          ],
          "intersectsDrawing": false,
          "fonts": [
            "NimbusRomNo9L-Regu"
          ],
          "sizes": [
            9.96
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "of leptons and quarks with unbroken SU(3)c ⊗U(1)em symmetry. These three C⊗O subalgebras",
          "bbox": [
            83.34,
            92.66,
            511.94,
            107.84
          ],
          "intersectsDrawing": false,
          "fonts": [
            "CMR10",
            "CMSY10",
            "MSBM10",
            "NimbusRomNo9L-Regu",
            "NimbusRomNo9L-ReguItal"
          ],
          "sizes": [
            7.97,
            10.91
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "are not independent but share a common quaternionic subalgebra spanned by {1,e1,e14,e15}. The",
          "bbox": [
            83.34,
            109.8,
            511.94,
            122.09
          ],
          "intersectsDrawing": false,
          "fonts": [
            "CMMI10",
            "CMSY10",
            "NimbusRomNo9L-Regu",
            "NimbusRomNo9L-ReguItal"
          ],
          "sizes": [
            7.97,
            10.91
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "three intersecting octonion subalgebras together with the multiplication rules of their base elements",
          "bbox": [
            83.34,
            125.1,
            511.93,
            136.01
          ],
          "intersectsDrawing": false,
          "fonts": [
            "NimbusRomNo9L-Regu"
          ],
          "sizes": [
            10.91
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "may be represented by the three Fano planes in Figure 1. Each of the three octonionic subalgebras",
          "bbox": [
            83.34,
            140.01,
            511.93,
            150.92
          ],
          "intersectsDrawing": false,
          "fonts": [
            "NimbusRomNo9L-Regu"
          ],
          "sizes": [
            10.91
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "PoS(EPS-HEP2019)615",
          "bbox": [
            540.6,
            221.97,
            578.06,
            563.93
          ],
          "intersectsDrawing": false,
          "fonts": [
            "Courier"
          ],
          "sizes": [
            30.0
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Figure 1: Fano planes of three octonionic subalgebras in the sedenions.",
          "bbox": [
            154.59,
            266.19,
            440.69,
            276.24
          ],
          "intersectsDrawing": false,
          "fonts": [
            "NimbusRomNo9L-Medi",
            "NimbusRomNo9L-Regu"
          ],
          "sizes": [
            9.96
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "above generates via its adjoint left actions a copy of Cℓ(6). From each of these algebras one",
          "bbox": [
            83.34,
            289.34,
            511.94,
            302.88
          ],
          "intersectsDrawing": false,
          "fonts": [
            "CMMI10",
            "CMR10",
            "MSBM10",
            "NimbusRomNo9L-Regu"
          ],
          "sizes": [
            10.91
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "constructs SU(3)c and U(1)em generators as above. That is, each generation has its own copy of",
          "bbox": [
            83.34,
            306.62,
            511.94,
            319.42
          ],
          "intersectsDrawing": false,
          "fonts": [
            "CMR10",
            "NimbusRomNo9L-Regu",
            "NimbusRomNo9L-ReguItal"
          ],
          "sizes": [
            7.97,
            10.91
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "SU(3)c and U(1)em associated with it.",
          "bbox": [
            83.34,
            321.53,
            249.65,
            334.33
          ],
          "intersectsDrawing": false,
          "fonts": [
            "CMR10",
            "NimbusRomNo9L-Regu",
            "NimbusRomNo9L-ReguItal"
          ],
          "sizes": [
            7.97,
            10.91
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "2.1 Spinorial degrees of freedom",
          "bbox": [
            83.34,
            347.73,
            235.84,
            358.63
          ],
          "intersectsDrawing": false,
          "fonts": [
            "NimbusRomNo9L-Medi"
          ],
          "sizes": [
            10.91
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "The spinorial degrees of freedom and the weak force are not captured by C⊗O nor by C⊗S.",
          "bbox": [
            103.66,
            365.89,
            511.94,
            379.44
          ],
          "intersectsDrawing": false,
          "fonts": [
            "CMSY10",
            "MSBM10",
            "NimbusRomNo9L-Regu"
          ],
          "sizes": [
            10.91
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "There are several ways to include these additional degrees of freedom. In [2] they are added by",
          "bbox": [
            83.34,
            383.43,
            511.94,
            394.34
          ],
          "intersectsDrawing": false,
          "fonts": [
            "NimbusRomNo9L-Regu"
          ],
          "sizes": [
            10.91
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "including a copy of the complex quaternions C⊗H, for an overall model based on C⊗H⊗O (as",
          "bbox": [
            83.34,
            395.7,
            511.94,
            409.25
          ],
          "intersectsDrawing": false,
          "fonts": [
            "CMSY10",
            "MSBM10",
            "NimbusRomNo9L-Regu"
          ],
          "sizes": [
            10.91
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "in [1]). The left adjoint algebra in this case is (C⊗H⊗O)L = Cℓ(8), the same as the left adjoint",
          "bbox": [
            83.34,
            410.6,
            511.94,
            425.53
          ],
          "intersectsDrawing": false,
          "fonts": [
            "CMMI10",
            "CMR10",
            "CMSY10",
            "MSBM10",
            "NimbusRomNo9L-Regu",
            "NimbusRomNo9L-ReguItal"
          ],
          "sizes": [
            7.97,
            10.91
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "algebra of C⊗S. In [11] on the other hand, all the degrees of freedom are included by considering",
          "bbox": [
            83.34,
            425.51,
            511.94,
            439.05
          ],
          "intersectsDrawing": false,
          "fonts": [
            "CMSY10",
            "MSBM10",
            "NimbusRomNo9L-Regu"
          ],
          "sizes": [
            10.91
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "all eight minimal left ideals of Cℓ(6), instead of just two as in [2, 10]. An alternative way of",
          "bbox": [
            83.34,
            440.41,
            511.93,
            453.96
          ],
          "intersectsDrawing": false,
          "fonts": [
            "CMMI10",
            "CMR10",
            "MSBM10",
            "NimbusRomNo9L-Regu"
          ],
          "sizes": [
            10.91
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "describing the full degrees of freedom is to therefore consider all 16 minimal left ideals of Cℓ(8).",
          "bbox": [
            83.34,
            455.32,
            507.92,
            468.86
          ],
          "intersectsDrawing": false,
          "fonts": [
            "CMMI10",
            "CMR10",
            "MSBM10",
            "NimbusRomNo9L-Regu"
          ],
          "sizes": [
            10.91
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Including a copy of the quaternions into the sedenion model would enlarge the left adjoint",
          "bbox": [
            103.66,
            472.86,
            511.93,
            483.77
          ],
          "intersectsDrawing": false,
          "fonts": [
            "NimbusRomNo9L-Regu"
          ],
          "sizes": [
            10.91
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "algebra to (C⊗H⊗S)L ∼= Cℓ10. Associated with this algebra is the group Spin(10), which forms",
          "bbox": [
            83.34,
            484.37,
            511.94,
            499.91
          ],
          "intersectsDrawing": false,
          "fonts": [
            "CMMI10",
            "CMR10",
            "CMSY10",
            "MSBM10",
            "NimbusRomNo9L-Regu",
            "NimbusRomNo9L-ReguItal"
          ],
          "sizes": [
            7.97,
            10.91
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "the basis of the SO(10) grand uniﬁed theory. It is however not clear why a copy of the octonions",
          "bbox": [
            83.34,
            502.41,
            511.94,
            513.57
          ],
          "intersectsDrawing": false,
          "fonts": [
            "CMR10",
            "NimbusRomNo9L-Regu",
            "NimbusRomNo9L-ReguItal"
          ],
          "sizes": [
            10.91
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "is missing in this case. Including a copy of the octonions, one gets (C ⊗H ⊗O ⊗S)L ∼= Cℓ(16),",
          "bbox": [
            83.34,
            514.18,
            511.94,
            529.72
          ],
          "intersectsDrawing": false,
          "fonts": [
            "CMMI10",
            "CMR10",
            "CMSY10",
            "MSBM10",
            "NimbusRomNo9L-Regu",
            "NimbusRomNo9L-ReguItal"
          ],
          "sizes": [
            7.97,
            10.91
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "which contains the e8 ⊕e8 algebra of the anomoly free 10D heterotic string [12].",
          "bbox": [
            83.34,
            532.08,
            434.94,
            545.02
          ],
          "intersectsDrawing": false,
          "fonts": [
            "CMSY10",
            "NimbusRomNo9L-Regu",
            "NimbusRomNo9L-ReguItal"
          ],
          "sizes": [
            7.97,
            10.91
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "3. The intersectionality of three generations as a basis for CKM mixing",
          "bbox": [
            83.34,
            563.88,
            446.63,
            575.84
          ],
          "intersectsDrawing": false,
          "fonts": [
            "NimbusRomNo9L-Medi"
          ],
          "sizes": [
            11.96
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "The three Fano planes in Figure 1 share a common complex quaternionic line of intersection.",
          "bbox": [
            103.66,
            590.86,
            511.94,
            601.77
          ],
          "intersectsDrawing": false,
          "fonts": [
            "NimbusRomNo9L-Regu"
          ],
          "sizes": [
            10.91
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "This reﬂects the fact that the three generations in the sedenion model are not independent of one",
          "bbox": [
            83.34,
            605.76,
            511.93,
            616.67
          ],
          "intersectsDrawing": false,
          "fonts": [
            "NimbusRomNo9L-Regu"
          ],
          "sizes": [
            10.91
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "another. This leads to unphysical transformations between generations not observed in nature such",
          "bbox": [
            83.34,
            620.67,
            511.93,
            631.58
          ],
          "intersectsDrawing": false,
          "fonts": [
            "NimbusRomNo9L-Regu"
